{
  "issue": 2841,
  "what": "Every verb the deploy gate runs, and all it runs (scripts/vps/gate/GateRules.ps1 reads this). A verb is one script of main, run on the box by the gate broker from a checkout of origin/main, with only the parameters named here. A parameter's rule is 'switch' (no value), 'text' (the text rule below) or a pattern its value must match whole. 'fixed' goes on every run of that verb; a fixed word with no hyphen is the value of the fixed parameter before it, so a verb can be held to one channel. 'build': true marks a live verb: its line must name main's full commit with -Build, and the broker runs it only when main is at exactly that commit (the build Patrick gave his word for); -Build never reaches the script. 'out' is the parameter that names the folder the verb writes its files into: the broker sets it to a folder of the run's own and sends back what lands there.",
  "text": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9 .,:;'()!?_+-]{0,159}$",
